Author: Neil Kao (UST Global Inc) <v-nientzukao@microsoft.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 17:09:04 2026 +0800

    zh-TW patch 033: localize QuasiSpace portal waypoint hover + CJK-safe star names
    
    Adds a localizable format template + CJK-aware nearest-star name lookup for
    the QuasiSpace-side portal hover text in pstarmap.c's DrawCursor() branch.
    
    Before:
      pstarmap.c hardcoded snprintf() English literal
        "[%c] To %05.1f : %05.1f (Near %.12s)"
      with GAME_STRING(nearest_star->Postfix) which returned raw English postfix
      ("Lyrae", "Squidi"). CJK players saw the whole string in English.
    
    After:
      fmt = GAME_STRING(PORTAL_WAYPOINT_FMT_INDEX);
      if (empty) fmt = "[%c] To %05.1f : %05.1f (Near %.12s)";  // English fallback
      snprintf(..., extracted_cjk_star_name);
    
    Changes:
    
      src/uqm/gamestr.h
        - New count define: ZHTW_TEMPLATE_STRING_COUNT (= 1 slot for now).
        - New enum base: ZHTW_TEMPLATE_BASE = STAR_POSTFIX_ZH_BASE + STAR_POSTFIX_ZH_COUNT
          (absolute index 1024 + 149 = 1173).
        - New index macro: PORTAL_WAYPOINT_FMT_INDEX (= ZHTW_TEMPLATE_BASE + 0).
        - GAMESTR_COUNT extended to cover the new slot.
    
      src/uqm/planets/pstarmap.c
        - Added forward declaration for existing static ExtractPureZh() so it can
          be called from DrawCursor()'s portal branch above its definition.
        - Rewrote the portal-hover snprintf branch:
            1. Read STAR_POSTFIX_ZH_BASE + postfixIdx to get "English（中文）"
               alias, then ExtractPureZh() to obtain just the CJK part.
            2. Fall back to raw English postfix (GAME_STRING(postfixIdx)) when
               the alias slot is empty or malformed (non-zh builds).
            3. Skip the byte-index vowel-drop abbreviation when the resulting
               name contains any non-ASCII byte — CJK names are already short
               and mid-cutting UTF-8 sequences produced garbage glyphs.
            4. Load format template from GAME_STRING(PORTAL_WAYPOINT_FMT_INDEX),
               falling back to the original English literal on empty.
    
    Impact on non-zh players:
      - GAME_STRING lookups at the two new indices return NULL/empty on the
        upstream content pack, so both fallbacks fire and the branch behaves
        exactly like before (identical to shipped upstream text).
    
    Impact on zh-TW addon players (Chinese displayed):
      - Format template becomes "[%c] 往 %05.1f : %05.1f（近 %s）".
      - Nearest star name becomes pure CJK (e.g. "天琴座", "半人馬座").
      - Full example: "[E] 往 191.0 : 92.6（近天琴座）"
    
    Content-side companion changes live in the zh-TW-addon repo:
      - _append_star_postfix_zh.py extended to emit ZHTW_TEMPLATE slot at index 1173.
      - translations/gamestrings.zh-TW.json gains _ZHTW_TEMPLATE_PORTAL_WAYPOINT_FMT.
      - _stage_hd_fonts rebuilt to include the 32 CJK constellation glyphs
        (琴/奎/獅/鯨/麒/麟/鳳/蠍/…) that were missing from the previous stage.
    
    Patch file: uqm-work/patches/033-pstarmap-portal-waypoint-fmt.patch

